research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-112-| Proposed result | Required inputs and proof work | Failure if omitted |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-113-|---|---|---|
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-114-| Defect charge/deformation theorem | A precise current equation or an axiomatically supplied topological defect; Stokes’ theorem on an interpolating chain disjoint from charged insertions; contact terms at operator insertions; boundary terms and current improvements; specified support regularity. | A slogan that “conserved current means symmetry” does not prove a topological defect in the quantum model. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md:115:| Finite 2-group background consistency | \(G,A,\rho,\beta\), normalized cocycle, twisted cochains and cup products, explicit degree conventions, and gauge transformations. Verify the cocycle condition, closure, composition, and invariance of \(\delta_a B=a^*\beta\). | Confusing the Postnikov coupling with an anomaly, omitting local coefficients, or using an untwisted \(\delta\) invalidates the background. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-116-| Categorical fusion/defect realization | The actual QFT or finite lattice Hamiltonian; construction of every defect operator; junction vector spaces; associator maps and pentagon; orientation reversal/adjoints; proof of isotopy invariance and of the claimed fusion coefficients. | Abstract fusion-category axioms or a transfer matrix do not show that any given QFT has those defects. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-117-| Finite gauging/gluing | The exact finite field groupoid and automorphism weights; cocycle action and triangulation convention; gauge invariance; gluing/sewing; boundary data and orientation signs. | A raw sum over field representatives can overcount gauge-equivalent data or fail to be local under gluing. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-118-| Perturbative anomaly/counterterm theorem | The selected non-Abelian action, fermion representations, local BRST differential, scheme/regulator and quantum Ward identity; prove the anomaly is a local cocycle and identify allowed counterterms; fix the invariant polynomial and descent normalization. | The current Abelian scalar proposition assumes locality/nilpotence/allowed counterterms and proves only an abstract obstruction equivalence. It does not prove a quantum action principle or identify the physical coefficient. |
