research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-127-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-128-The published mathematical library supplies enough to start, but not a complete generalized-anomaly engine. Keep new pure mathematics local to the new category or reuse exact canonical root IDs. Do not create physical dependencies in **items/**.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-129-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md:130:1. **Higher-group cochains:** ordinary group cohomology and Postnikov towers exist, but the selected twisted 2-group background equation, its local coefficients, cup products, cochain homotopies, Bockstein/Pontryagin-square conventions, and finite gauge-equivalence groupoid need a local explicit contract and proofs. For continuous backgrounds, differential cocycles/characters and their products are a separate missing supplier.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-131-2. **Defect higher categories:** ordinary monoidal/fusion and weak 2-category foundations exist. A physical network on stratified \(d\)-manifolds still needs a chosen defect codimension, labels on each stratum, junction spaces, orientation/dual data, associators and higher coherence. The physical category-to-fusion-data dictionary is not supplied by \(2\mathrm{Vect}_G^\omega\) or \(\mathrm{Mod}(\mathcal C)\) alone.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-132-3. **Global/torsion topology:** ordinary cohomology, oriented bordism of maps, spin structures, Dirac index, characteristic classes, and some Thom-spectrum results exist. A category-level anomaly classification needs the exact spin/orientation structure with a \(BG\) or higher-group background, the corresponding bordism spectrum and computation, and a proof relating its invariants to the physical determinant/anomaly theory. The available oriented \(\Omega_*^{SO}(X)\) item and real Chern–Weil classes are insufficient by themselves.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md-133-4. **QFT definition/functoriality:** selected free local algebras and finite BF/RT models exist. General interacting QFT on manifolds with corners/defect strata, background gauge-field dependence, boundary conditions and gluing is not a current universal supplier. Each theorem must name its selected model rather than use “QFT” as a proof assumption with no carrier.
--
